# PC-01 web shell environment.
#
# Copy to `web/.env.local` (git-ignored) before `npm run dev`. Next loads it into
# `process.env` for both halves of this app — the browser bundle and the Node server — and
# the difference between the two halves is the whole reason this file has two sections.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PUBLIC. Compiled into the browser bundle, so nothing secret may go here.
#
# Next inlines every `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` reference at build time. `web/src/shared/config/env.ts`
# says so in its own comment, and `web/tests/guards/server-credential.guard.test.ts`
# refuses any `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` name that reads as a secret.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Required. The base path the browser calls. There is deliberately no localhost default in
# code: a missing value fails loudly at first use rather than silently pointing a build at
# a developer's laptop.
#
# `/bff/v1` is this app's OWN server-side route (`src/app/bff/v1/[...path]/route.ts`),
# which attaches `T-6`'s bearer credential and forwards to the API. It is a RELATIVE path,
# so the bundle names no origin and the same build works behind any host.
#
# Pointing this at `/api/v1` instead makes the browser call the API directly, with no
# credential, and every one of the twelve operations answers 401. That is what the
# deployed alpha did before `W15-AUTH`.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=/bff/v1

# Optional. Label shown in the shell header so an operator can tell two local
# instances apart. Cosmetic only; authorizes nothing.
NEXT_PUBLIC_INSTANCE_LABEL=local

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER-ONLY. Read by the Node process, never by the browser.
#
# Neither name carries the `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix, so Next does not inline either one: in a
# module that reaches the client, an environment lookup for a name without that prefix
# compiles to a lookup on an empty object. Both are read in exactly one module,
# `src/shared/config/server-env.ts`, which only the `/bff/v1` route handler imports.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Required by the forward. The absolute origin the Next SERVER reaches the API on. In the
# alpha stack this is the compose service name, which does not resolve in a browser and
# never needs to. A relative value is refused: it would make the server forward to itself.
AUDITMANAGER_API_UPSTREAM=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# Required by the forward. THE CREDENTIAL. The same value the API container reads under the
# same name — one deployment secret handed to two processes. Fail-closed: with this unset,
# `/bff/v1` answers `401 authentication_required` rather than forwarding uncredentialed.
#
#   python3 -c 'import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))'
#
# The value below authorizes nothing and is not a secret.
AUDITMANAGER_API_TOKEN=local-disposable-example-token
